# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Agent rule

Start by reading [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) at the repo root. It is the
canonical spec-for-agents for this project — project context, stack, conventions,
design-token pipeline, and how to work with `DESIGN.md` and `IMPLEMENT.web.md`.

## When to follow a maintenance runbook

When the user's intent matches one of these, read the named runbook in full
and follow it — do not improvise.

| Intent | Runbook |
| --- | --- |
| Sync tokens, propagate a `DESIGN.md` or `IMPLEMENT.web.md` change, rebuild the CSS/Tailwind theme, refresh the Figma library from code | [`.agents/runbooks/sync-tokens.md`](../../.agents/runbooks/sync-tokens.md) |
| Push tokens to Figma, create or rebuild the design library, add a Figma file to a project that has never had one | [`.agents/runbooks/figma-library-push.md`](../../.agents/runbooks/figma-library-push.md) |

## Capability boundary

The runbooks assume the agent can execute shell commands, run `npx`, and call
the Figma MCP. In Cursor, the Cursor agent has all three. Follow the runbook
step by step; do not paraphrase or shortcut.
